      "updated_at": "2023-05-01T21:02:35Z",
      "body": "The issue with the `lambda` is you have no visibility into the return value of the task, which is a result-handle. For use in a view (fire-and-forget) this is not so important, but we don't want to preclude that use-case entirely. So Huey provides a more ergonomic method which has the benefit of:\r\n\r\n1. Freeing you from registering callbacks and closing over arguments\r\n2. Providing meaningful return value, the result-handle",
      "author_association": "OWNER",
      "pin": null,
